From f6e47a55bfbec73db3f5a5f2ebd03f8b182aa37c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:24:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom_iommu: unwind clocks after failed runtime resume

Runtime resume enables the bulk clock reference before resetting a
non-secure IOMMU or restoring secure configuration. Both error returns
leave that reference held. Release the clocks on either failure and
preserve the original error. Keep the successful resume/suspend contract.

Source-extracted tests cover both formats, VFE-style bank IDs 0/1/2,
allocation and every secure-restore failure, successful publication and
resume/suspend. The baseline fails 23 of 52 cases; both repairs leave zero.
Three deliberate regressions are rejected by their intended contracts.
Kernel services, secure firmware and context programming are modeled.
Normal LeakSanitizer and fail-fast ASan/UBSan remain enabled.

Codex prepared this new local repair and host qualification. Thirteen
selected native objects pass with nonpermissive CFI on supported ARM,
ARM64 and ARM64 RT profiles; MMCC remains native ARM32 only. Original
source/board attribution is retained. Human review, security review and
DCO remain pending; no sign-off certification or hardware claim is made.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 925967662fb1..8dc4e510cbc2 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -1168,11 +1168,11 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_iommu_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (qcom_iommu->non_secure) {
 		ret = qcom_iommu_reset_ns(qcom_iommu);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			goto err_disable_clks;
 	} else if (dev->pm_domain) {
 		ret = qcom_scm_restore_sec_cfg(qcom_iommu->sec_id, 0);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			goto err_disable_clks;
 	}
 
 	qcom_iommu_bfb_setup(qcom_iommu);
@@ -1187,6 +1187,10 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_iommu_resume(struct device *dev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	return 0;
+
+err_disable_clks:
+	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(CLK_NUM, qcom_iommu->clks);
 	return ret;
 }
 
